---
description: SpeechSearch conventions (Hebrew RTL, Supabase RLS, repo layer)
alwaysApply: true
---
- Read `CLAUDE.md` in the repo root first; it lists the project rules.
- Hebrew UI, feminine address, RTL: use logical Tailwind utilities (`ms-`/`pe-`/`start-`/`end-`).
- Data only through `lib/data` (`repo`); implement every method in both `supabase.ts` and `demo.ts`.
- Database changes = new migration file in `supabase/migrations`, with RLS. Do not edit old migrations.
- Secrets never in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, never in the repo, never pasted into chat. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
- Plan mode first for large changes; run `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run build` before finishing.
